cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Performance variability of neural network training on MNIST and YOLO object detection: training and analysis code"
abstract: >-
  Training and analysis code to study how the test accuracy of a neural
  network varies across hundreds of training runs that differ only in the
  random seed. Eight architectures, from a single-layer perceptron to a
  14-layer CNN, are trained on MNIST, together with a hyperparameter ablation
  and an overfitting experiment. The analysis scripts estimate the
  distribution of results of each model and the probability that a given
  number of runs misranks two models (Monte Carlo and Bootstrap), together
  with survival functions of the results and an ANOVA of the ablation grid;
  the same analyses are applied to YOLOv8 object-detection results on COCO
  and on the KAIST and LLVIP multispectral datasets, trained with the
  companion repository yolo_test_utils. A cross-GPU replication study
  re-trains six MNIST conditions with a common seed pool on several GPU
  architectures and software stacks, and a further script builds the public
  per-trial data deposit of the article.
